<title>USA: Columbia Gas says deal to boost reserves.</title>
<headline>Columbia Gas says deal to boost reserves.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Columbia Gas System Inc said Tuesday that its deal to acquire Alamco Inc will boost reserves to 800 billion cubic feet of gas.</p>
<p>The purchase will be made by Columbia Natural Resources Inc, a unit of Columbia Gas System.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Columbia said, holders of outstanding Alamco stock, options and warrants would receive in cash $15.75 per share of common stock.</p>
<p>The purchase price, assuming the exercise and cash-out of all warrants and options, is about $101 million, of which about $18 million involves the assumption of Alamco debt by Columbia Natural Resources.</p>
</text>
